VCutsceneCamera: bound the trajectory and target keyframe counts.

`VCutsceneCamera::load` reads `numPos` and `numTargets` off the file and
validates neither:

	this->position_count = r.read_int();  // numPos
	this->target_count = r.read_int();    // numTargets

	for (auto i = 0; i < this->position_count; ++i) {
		auto obj = r.read_object<VCameraTrajectoryFrame>(version);
		this->trajectory_frames.push_back(obj);
	}

The same shape as the waynet counts patch 0037 bounds, with one difference that
makes it worse rather than better: there is no `reserve` here at all, so the
"an absurd count is the harmless one" escape hatch every other patch in this
series relies on -- `reserve` throwing `bad_alloc` before the loop is entered --
does not exist. Every value is a merely large one. And the loop cannot stop on
its own for patch 0033's reason: `ReadArchive::read_object` past the end of the
entry stream logs "Expected object, got entry" and returns null rather than
throwing, and nothing in this reader dereferences a frame.

Measured on the unpatched reader against `zenkit-node`'s 6 KB camera fixture
with `numPos` rewritten in place to 0x0FFFFFFF: 268 million null keyframes,
4.33 GB resident, and the world still reports LOADED after 15.8 s. `numTargets`
is the same, 15.5 s.

A negative count is refused too, and it is the one value that "works" unpatched:
both loops are `i < count` over a signed `int`, so an on-disk 0xFFFFFFFF loads a
cutscene camera with no keyframes at all instead of failing -- a world ZenGin
would not have written, read as if it were fine.

Both counts are bounded by the bytes actually left in the reader, with the same
`_bytes_remaining` helper and the same four-byte per-object floor as `Mesh.cc`,
`BspTree.cc` and `WayNet.cc`. The floor is under the smallest header any of the
three archive formats can write, because a bound must never refuse a world the
engine loads.

Not found by `zenkit-node/tools/fuzz-world.js --counts`, and it could not have
been: the sweep only reaches the INTEGER entries its fixture carries, and the
golden `minimal.g2.zen` has no cutscene camera. The `camera` fixture variant
(`zenkit-node/src/fixture.cc`) was authored for it, which is the same shape as
the `npc` variant patches 0040 and 0041 needed.

